=> gate check: does each gap member contain a mult of its loose-denominator 2N+1?
   AND a mult of its tight-denominator N+1 (=13 at N=12)? The two-gate threading.

At N=12 the two gates are mod-13 (=N+1, prime) and mod-25 (=2N+1=5^2). A gap member needs
both. The width 1/(13*25)=1/325 = the product => threading both is maximally tight, and the
n-specific closure is that at N=12 NO 12-family threads both simultaneously (fleet-verified empty).
